# HTTP API & Dashboard

## Server

- `ApiServer` on `localhost:7777` — read-only state + settings PATCH. No remote bind.
- Research DevTree is separate (`localhost:7778`, Research project only).

## JSON conventions

- `JsonSerializerOptions` with `PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase`.
- Return structured errors: `{ "error": "..." }` with appropriate HTTP status.
- Wrap handlers in try/catch; never leak stack traces to clients in production paths.

## State endpoints

Publish snapshots from `RadarApp` (`/state`, `/entities`, `/landmarks`) — **do not** trigger heavy reads from API handlers. API reads cached `_state` / stores.

## Settings PATCH

- Apply known fields via switch/case; collect `applied` list; call `_settings.Save()` only when something changed.
- Validate/clamp numeric inputs (`Math.Clamp`) server-side — same bounds as ImGui sliders.

## Dashboard HTML

`DashboardHtml.cs` is large but intentional — keep JS/CSS inline consistent with existing patterns. New settings need matching form controls + hotkey capture (keyboard + pad).

## Icons API

`/api/icons` serves shape library for dashboard pickers; built-ins from `IconLibrary`, overrides from `icons/*.svg` next to exe.
